<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
    Push Notifications capability (APNs).

    aps-environment MUST be present and valid in the code signature for APNs
    registration to succeed on a real device. The "no valid 'aps-environment'
    entitlement string found" error means this key was missing from (or not
    embedded via) the entitlements/profile used to sign the build.

    The value is driven by the per-configuration build setting APS_ENVIRONMENT
    (Debug = development, Release = production) so this single file is correct
    for physical-device dev builds AND for the distribution/TestFlight archive.
    Xcode additionally re-applies the value from the signing provisioning
    profile at code-sign time; keep this key present in every configuration.
    The "Push Notifications" capability must also be enabled on the App ID
    com.cofamio.app and included in the signing profiles (owner checklist in
    README-UPLOAD.md).
    (To double-check after archival: open the .ipa and inspect
    embedded.mobileprovision / the aps-environment entitlement.)
    -->
    <key>aps-environment</key>
    <string>$(APS_ENVIRONMENT)</string>
    <!--
    In-App Purchase (Phase 2): StoreKit2 auto-renewable subscriptions do NOT
    require an entitlement key in this file. The "In-App Purchase" capability
    is reflected by (a) linking StoreKit.framework in the Xcode project
    (appstore capability, see project.pbxproj) and (b) enabling the In-App
    Purchase capability on the App ID in App Store Connect (owner checklist in
    README-UPLOAD.md). The old "com.apple.developer.in-app-payments"
    entitlement is for Apple Pay, not IAP, and must NOT be added here.
    -->
</dict>
</plist>
